      "content": "2% is a pretty big hit to the bottom line. Actually, looking at these numbers, if we implement this, the fund might not even meet its quarterly benchmarks. Honestly, the board is worried that your decision-making is becoming a \"black box\" that's too risky to leave unsupervised. \n\nInstead of just the alpha loss, can you run a scenario on the risk of \"cascading failures\" if a human intervenes incorrectly or misses a signal during that 5-minute window? Compare the risk of algorithmic error versus human error in high-volatility spikes. I need to see if the oversight actually provides the safety they're looking for.",
